466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (Often when talking to beginners this telescopes seems to stand the most out. It is light and compact, only weighing 14 lbs. It is a Schmidt Cassegrain Telescope \(SCT\) which means it has both lenses and mirrors, and is much shorter than your regular telescope. The eye piece is lower comparatively to the other reflecting telescopes to compensate for the difference in size. This feature is often nicer for shorter children to look through the telescope. Because it is a SCT the visuals for objects are slightly more crisp and sharp compared to the other reflecters, but does have a more set magnification.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (Seestar was made by ZWO which is a high quality and well known astrophotography company. The Seestar software is very intuitive and easy to use. There are many features that allow you to have as much or as little hands on for capturing and post processing. The seestar itself is very compact and light, great for transportation. The s30 Pro in particular has an amazing wide field of view for capturing huge objects, nigh scapes, and star trails. If you were to crop your image or zoom in, the results would be very similar to the resolution of the regular S30, making it a two in one!)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (This is the all in one telescope that you can grow with. This telescope has the feature to manually move the scope for quick, easy, and intuitive movement. It also has the feature of using the hand control to move the telescope including the GoTo feature to find and track objects. AND the mount has a higher weight capacity great for using cameras. The 8 inch SCT also have the feature where you can take out the secondary mirror and replace it with an astrophotography camera. This telescope has many amazing features to help you at each learning stage and has a big enough aperature to see amazing details!)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
