556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (There are two basic telescopes types,  refractors and reflectors. Refracting telescopes utilizes lenses to bend incoming light straight towards the eyepiece. Reflecting telescopes utilizes multiple mirrors to reflect light to the eyepiece.  Now a little nicer types of telescopes are Schmidt-Cassegrain telescopes \(SCT\) and Maksutov telescopes. SCT have both features of a refracting and reflecting telescopes as it bends and folds light to have a huge focal length in a compact tube. These offer great details and higher magnification. Maksutov telescopes also refract and reflect light but have a thicker lens and curved secondary mirror to obtain more contrasting details specifically for planets.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
