560 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (There are different types of mounts you can put your telescope on. Altitude/Azimuth is the most basic as they move up and down and left to right. Dobsonians too move like ALT/AZ but they sit on a table or the ground on a turn table like mount. Stepping it up there are equatorial mounts. EQ mounts are made to follow the motion of the sky and counter the Earths rotation and use right ascension and declination. These too are coordinates like ALT/AZ but are measured in time and degrees! Lastly there are computerized mounts. These mounts can only be moved with a hand controller but have the wonderful capability of finding objects and tracking them for you. By inserting the time, date, and location, then successfully doing a three star alignment where you center three distant and bright stars in the eyepiece, the telescope will know where it is and will give you a list of objects that are viewable that night! When choosing an object the telescope will instantly move to find your object and track it! )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
