612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 286 0 R
/T (It is important to understand the difference between magnification and detail. Detail comes from how much light is let into the telescope. Bigger aperature telescopes are going to give more detail, and will expand the number of objects you can see, as many objects like galaxies and star clusters are dim. Magnification is provided from the eyepieces you use. They allow the ability to increase and decrease your field of view similar to zooming in and out. You will not be able to increse the detail you see by changing the magnification.)
/E (It is important to understand the difference between magnification and detail. Detail comes from how much light is let into the telescope. Bigger aperature telescopes are going to give more detail, and will expand the number of objects you can see, as many objects like galaxies and star clusters are dim. Magnification is provided from the eyepieces you use. They allow the ability to increase and decrease your field of view similar to zooming in and out. You will not be able to increse the detail you see by changing the magnification.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
