807 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 291 0 R
/E (Schmidt-Cassegrain telescopes are an all time favorite. They range from 5 inches to 16 inches and also give high quality imaging similar to the Maksutov-Cassegrain telescopes. The glass for SCTs are a bit easier to make comparatively to the Maksutov- Cassegrain telescopes, making bigger sizes easier to find. In comparison to newtonian reflectors, SCTs are more compact. They also have more set in place optics so you rarely if not at all have to collimate them. SCTs also have a higher base in magnification and narrower fields of view. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
808 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 291 0 R
/E (Edge HD telescopes are a special type of Schmidt-Cassegrain telescope. They often have built in correctors to fix off-axis coma and field curvature. This gives you more sharp and flat field stars all the way to the edge of your field of view. Edge HD telescopes have amazing optics for viewing and are great if you have a particular prefference for perfect stars. Often times Edge HD telescopes are used for astrophotography because of their flat field aspect. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
