2159 0 obj
<<
/Title (It is important to understand the difference between magnification and detail. Detail comes from how much light is let into the telescope. Bigger aperature telescopes are going to give more detail, and will expand the number of objects you can see, as many objects like galaxies and star clusters are dim. Magnification is provided from the eyepieces you use. They allow the ability to increase and decrease your field of view similar to zooming in and out. You will not be able to increse the detail you see by changing the magnification.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2137 0 R
/Next 2160 0 R
>>
endobj
2160 0 obj
<<
/Title (Eyepieces are counter intuitive. Bigger millimeter eyepieces will give you less magnification, and smaller millimeter eyepeices will give you higher magnification.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2137 0 R
/Prev 2159 0 R
>>
endobj
